# UI & Design Guidelines

## 1. Composition over Reinvention
- ALWAYS use official shadcn/ui components before writing custom markup.
- Dashboard views must be composed of `Sidebar`, `Card`, `Table`, `Badge`, and `Tabs`.
- For notifications/alerts, use `sonner` or `Alert`—never write custom floating banners.
- Use `lucide-react` for all icons. Icons inside buttons must use semantic sizes (`size-4`).

## 2. Strict Layout & Spacing Rules
- Never use arbitrary pixel values like `p-[17px]` or `gap-[13px]`. Follow standard 4-point spacing (`gap-2`, `gap-4`, `gap-6`, `p-4`, `p-6`).
- No `space-x-*` or `space-y-*`. Use flexbox or grid with explicit `gap-*`.
- For equal width/height, use `size-*` (e.g., `size-8` instead of `w-8 h-8`).
- Maintain visual hierarchy: 1 primary action per view, distinct section headers, and muted text for labels (`text-muted-foreground`).

## 3. Dark Theme / Color Palette
- Strict semantic color tokens only: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`.
- NEVER hardcode arbitrary colors (e.g., `bg-[#1a1a1a]` or raw `bg-zinc-800` inside components). Rely entirely on CSS variable tokens defined in `globals.css`.
- Keep accent colors to roughly 10% of the screen (status badges, active buttons, metric graphs).